# The fixtures are captured from zsh byte for byte, and several hold bytes
# that are not text at all -- a lone \r among them.  Git's Windows default
# rewrites line endings on checkout, which corrupts them: a subject recorded
# as `readme` comes back as `readme\r` and stops matching `readme`.
#
# So no fixture is ever converted, and the rest of the tree is normalised to
# LF in the repository whatever the checkout does.
* text=auto eol=lf

test/fixtures/** -text
*.txt -text
